{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-1r5.1:000001:issue_created:sase-1r5.1:71af704c33c89fd37dc392f439cb52a053f83deee6510146958abba650ad2a12","timestamp":"2026-11-04T11:54:52Z","actor":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-1r5","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"sase-1r5.1","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"sase-1r5.1","title":"Retry transient GitHub SSH publickey denials on git network operations","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":"sase-1r5","owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-11-04T11:54:52Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-1r5","updated_at":"2026-11-04T11:54:52Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"A GitHub-side burst of `Permission denied (publickey)` rejections of valid SSH keys no longer aborts agent launches or background git jobs. Launch-blocking and background git network operations retry such denials within a bounded, deadline-aware budget. Genuine credential failures still surface promptly as permanent authentication errors that keep the original stderr: deploy-key refusals, a host with no local SSH credential at all, and a denial that outlasts the budget.","design":"plan:202611/github_publickey_retry.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Approved epic plan plan:202611/github_publickey_retry.md requests this work","dependencies":[]}}}
{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-1r5.1:000002:issue_created:sase-1r5.1.1:a6fc945f2bb0fd7988775592b9d3bfacd34668a374c8ed800f994c48bb4fbc78","timestamp":"2026-11-04T11:54:52Z","actor":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-1r5","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"sase-1r5.1.1","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"sase-1r5.1.1","title":"sase-core credential_unconfirmed verdict for SSH publickey denials","status":"open","issue_type":"phase","parent_id":"sase-1r5.1","owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-11-04T11:54:52Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-1r5","updated_at":"2026-11-04T11:54:52Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"core-verdict: in sase-core, classify SSH publickey denials on git and git_clone operations as a new non-retryable `credential_unconfirmed` verdict whose reason keeps the `authentication` category. Deploy-key refusals stay permanent, the retryability module becomes a facade, and table and parity tests cover the new verdict.","design":"","model":"","size":"medium","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Epic plan plan:202611/github_publickey_retry.md defines phase core-verdict as one work unit","dependencies":[]}}}
